Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:31:02 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 21/26] ling: kept prompt states in place
 (TF_LING_KEEP_INPLACE=auto|on|off, auto past the native window): a kept state
 holds the KDA part alone and names its slot's cache rows; a forward writing
 below a state's position drops it first, a freed slot copies its states out
 (their old size); restore copies rows only across slots. kept.zig holds the
 kept-state code (engine.zig 553 lines). TP=1 trial pack: resumed at 9,000 ==
 fresh 9/9, byte-equal to the copied state's run

